 14	// A registry schema as Anthropic's strict mode accepts it: the keywords that
 15	// mode rejects (minimum, maximum, multipleOf, minLength, maxLength, maxItems,
 16	// minItems above 1, minProperties, maxProperties) move out of every node and
 17	// into that node's description, as "(minimum 1, maximum 100)". Everything
 18	// else is kept. The registry keeps the full schema, and native validation
 19	// still enforces every keyword before a call runs.
 20	nlohmann::json anthropic_strict_schema(const nlohmann::json& schema);
