 20	// The reads in flight. A read runs on a thread nothing joins, and Http's curl
 21	// is torn down with the process's statics; a read still inside curl then
 22	// would crash the exit. So the app's exit stops new reads and cancels those
 23	// in flight, and waits a moment for them to leave.
 24	struct Reads
 25	{
 26	    std::atomic<bool> stopping{false};
 27	    std::atomic<int>  running{0};
 28	};
